[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 764,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 701,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120698,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 701,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Mu heavy chain disease (HCD) is a systemic B-cell neoplasm with hepatosplenic, nodal, and bone involvement characterized by vacuolated plasma cells and secretion of defective serum mu heavy chains that lack associated light chains; free serum and/or urine kappa light chains may also be present.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 765,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 702,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120699,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 702,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>9762/3 Mu heavy chain disease</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 766,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 703,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120700,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 703,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>2A84.2 Mu heavy chain disease</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 767,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 704,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120701,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 704,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 768,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 705,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120702,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 705,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 769,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 706,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120703,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 706,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The spleen is almost universally involved, with hepatic involvement in 75% of patients, nodal disease in 40%, and bone marrow involvement in 20% {1566748; 24683718}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 770,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 707,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120704,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 707,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Bone involvement is characterized by lytic bone lesions. When associated with systemic illnesses such as amyloidosis or systemic lupus erythematosus, features of the underlying disorders are present. Anaemia is commonly present, with or without lymphocytosis, typically secondary to bone marrow infiltration by neoplastic cells {24683718}. Lymphocytosis is typically milder than that seen in chronic lymphocytic leukaemia {35932039}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 771,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 708,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120705,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 708,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Mu&nbsp;HCD is the rarest form of HCD. It shows a male predominance and occurs in the sixth decade of life.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 772,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 709,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120706,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 709,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>A few reported cases with <em>MYD88</em> p.L265P mutation suggests that at least some cases are biologically related to lymphoplasmacytic lymphoma (LPL) {35932039; 33596645}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 773,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 710,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120707,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 710,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Mu&nbsp;HCD arises from a clonal expansion of cells of B&nbsp;lineage producing truncated mu heavy chain that lacks light chain binding sites {9858149; 18036562}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 780,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 717,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120708,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 717,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 774,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 711,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120709,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 711,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Involved tissues are infiltrated by vacuolated plasma cells and small round lymphoid cells with mature chromatin, resembling cells of chronic lymphocytic leukaemia&nbsp;/ small lymphocytic lymphoma (CLL/SLL) or LPL {24683718; 28751360; 35932039}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 775,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 712,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120710,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 712,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>FNA may be used in association with core biopsy to sample splenic or liver lesions, acquire material for flow cytometry or other ancillary tests, and detect associated systemic amyloidosis.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 776,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 713,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120711,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 713,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Clonal IG gene rearrangements may be present with high levels of somatic hypermutation. <em>MYD88</em> p.L265P mutation has recently been reported in a subset of cases {35932039; 33596645}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 779,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 716,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120712,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 716,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> bone marrow or tissue involvement by IgM-positive small round lymphocytes and vacuolated plasma cells; elevated serum free kappa light chains or kappa Bence Jones proteinuria.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> serum immunofixation or other modality demonstrating anti-mu reactivity without associated light chain.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 777,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 714,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120713,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 714,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The modified Lugano staging system for underlying lymphoma (e.g. CLL/SLL, LPL) applies.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 778,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 715,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 120714,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 192,
        "headingId": 715,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>The prognosis is highly variable, with reported overall survival times ranging from &lt;&nbsp;1&nbsp;month to decades (median: 2&nbsp;years). Delays in diagnosis negatively impact survival. Watchful waiting without therapy is recommended for indolent, asymptomatic cases. In cases of active, symptomatic lymphoma, CLL/SLL-directed therapy (or LPL-directed therapy if <em>MYD88</em>-mutated) is indicated {24683718; 33596645}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T12:01:39"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]